From 076f523ebc5b4d37907244a8b91435da8eabd13e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:34:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] views: Keep app-modal dialogs inside their window on Wayland

CreateViewsJavaScriptDialog() moves a new app-modal dialog into the work
area of the display nearest to it. The check compares screen
coordinates. Wayland does not give clients global screen coordinates,
so Chrome assumes that a browser window has its origin at (0, 0). The
display, however, can have any origin in the compositor's layout.

If no display covers the window's assumed position, AdjustToFit() moves
the dialog by the display origin. On Wayland the dialog is a child of
the browser window, so this places it outside the window, where it is
never visible. The dialog is still window-modal, and the app-modal event
blocker sends no input to the other browser windows. Every Chrome window
then ignores the keyboard and the mouse until the user presses Escape
or Enter without seeing the dialog. A beforeunload dialog, for example
from closing a tab with unsaved changes, is enough to trigger this.

Skip the adjustment when the Ozone platform does not support global
screen coordinates. The constrained-window code already positions the
dialog relative to its parent window.

Test: On Wayland, with the only output at a non-zero logical position
(niri: `position x=3840 y=1800`), close a tab whose page has a
beforeunload handler. Before this change, the "Leave site?" dialog is
not visible and all windows ignore input. After it, the dialog is
centered at the top of the browser window.
---
 .../chrome_javascript_app_modal_view_factory_views.cc    | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_javascript_app_modal_view_factory_views.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_javascript_app_modal_view_factory_views.cc
index acd1517..027f394 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_javascript_app_modal_view_factory_views.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/chrome_javascript_app_modal_view_factory_views.cc
@@ -79,6 +79,15 @@ class ChromeJavaScriptAppModalDialogViews
 };
 
 void AdjustWidgetBoundsIfOffscreen(views::Widget* widget) {
+  // Without global screen coordinates (e.g. Wayland), the screen origin of
+  // the browser window is unknown, so the dialog bounds cannot be compared
+  // with a display's work area. Moving the dialog into that work area can
+  // place it outside its parent window, where it stays invisible while it
+  // blocks input to every browser window.
+  if (!constrained_window::SupportsGlobalScreenCoordinates()) {
+    return;
+  }
+
   gfx::Rect widget_bounds = widget->GetWindowBoundsInScreen();
   gfx::Rect screen_rect =
       display::Screen::Get()
